Observe the following Object-Oriented code utilizing constructors. What is the exact output?

```java
class Box {
    int width, height;
    Box() {
        this(5, 10);
    }
    Box(int w, int h) {
        this.width = w;
        this.height = h;
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Box b = new Box();
        System.out.println(b.width + "x" + b.height);
    }
}
```

Analyze the static variable behavior in the following code. What is the output?

```java
class Counter {
    static int count = 0;
    Counter() {
        count++;
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Counter c1 = new Counter();
        Counter c2 = new Counter();
        Counter c3 = new Counter();
        System.out.println(Counter.count);
    }
}
```

